# UPGRADE-15

# Local Model Factory & Auto-Tuning

# GGUF / llama.cpp First-Class Runtime,

# Ollama/vLLM Lifecycle, Model Registry,

# Safe Model Acquisition, Quantization Profiles,

# Automatic Hardware Tuning, Benchmark Tournament,

# Per-Project Model Profiles and Real Local-AI Proof

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-14.

PRIMARY PRINCIPLE:

NO-COST FIRST.

PAID PROVIDERS ARE OPTIONAL.

The main objective of Upgrade-15 is not to create more adapters.

The objective is to make ZCoder capable of answering:

"What is the best model that can ACTUALLY run on this machine,
for this coding task, with zero paid API usage?"

and then execute the job using that model.

============================================================
PHASE 0 — VERIFY UPGRADE-14
===========================

Upgrade-14 reportedly concluded:

CORE_FREE: PASS E3

LOCAL_MODEL_REAL: NOT_TESTED

Host:

Linux x86_64
8 logical CPU cores
18.49 GB RAM
12.76 GB available
CPU_ONLY
0 GB VRAM

Do not assume this remains true.

Run:

git status --short
git log -30 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -30

python -m pytest -q -ra

python main.py --version
python -m build
git diff --check

Run current release gate.

Inspect:

local_ai_stack.py
no_cost_platform.py
agent_runtime.py
release_gate.py
model/provider code
tests/
webapp/

Produce:

UPGRADE-14 REALITY MATRIX

Capability
Claim
Implementation
Mock Evidence
Real Runtime Evidence
Verdict

Use:

PROVEN
CONTRACT_ONLY
SIMULATED
NOT_TESTED
MISSING
INCORRECT

============================================================

1. CORRECT MODEL INVENTORY SEMANTICS
   ============================================================

Upgrade-14 listed models such as:

qwen2.5-coder:7b
llama3.3:70b
starcoder2:3b

but did not have a running Ollama daemon.

Therefore distinguish:

CATALOG_MODEL
DISCOVERED_MODEL
DOWNLOADED_MODEL
INSTALLED_MODEL
LOADED_MODEL
BENCHMARKED_MODEL

Never display a static catalog entry as installed.

============================================================
2. MODEL STATE MACHINE
======================

Create explicit state:

KNOWN
AVAILABLE_REMOTE
DOWNLOADING
DOWNLOADED
VERIFIED
LOADABLE
LOADED
FAILED
REMOVED

Do not derive state from filename alone.

============================================================
3. LOCAL MODEL FACTORY
======================

Create a coherent:

LocalModelFactory

responsible for:

discovery
metadata
acquisition planning
verification
runtime preparation
benchmarking
profile generation
selection
lifecycle

Do not put inference logic directly into the factory.

============================================================
4. RUNTIME ARCHITECTURE
=======================

Support first-class adapters:

LlamaCppRuntime
OllamaRuntime
VLLMRuntime
GenericOpenAICompatibleRuntime

Do not duplicate LocalAgentRuntime.

Architecture:

LocalAgentRuntime
│
LocalModelGateway
│
├── llama.cpp
├── Ollama
├── vLLM
└── Generic

============================================================
5. LLAMA.CPP FIRST-CLASS SUPPORT
================================

Audit the CURRENT official llama.cpp repository/server documentation at
execution time.

Implement documented functionality only.

Support where current server actually permits:

model information
chat
streaming
structured output
tool calling
embeddings
health/server metadata

Do not assume every loaded model supports every server feature.

============================================================
6. LLAMA.CPP DISCOVERY
======================

Detect:

llama
llama-server
legacy llama.cpp binaries if appropriate

Use:

PATH
configured executable
known local installation only

Do not scan arbitrary filesystem.

============================================================
7. LLAMA.CPP SERVER MANAGEMENT
==============================

ZCoder may manage a job-owned local server.

Support:

start
health
stop
crash detection

Bind loopback by default.

Do not expose:

0.0.0.0

unless explicitly configured.

============================================================
8. SERVER PROCESS SAFETY
========================

Persist:

PID
model
port
runtime
started_at
command fingerprint

On restart:

do not kill unrelated user process merely because PID was reused.

Verify process identity.

============================================================
9. DYNAMIC PORT ALLOCATION
==========================

Avoid hardcoded shared ports.

Use configured or available local port.

Prevent two ZCoder model servers from colliding.

============================================================
10. MODEL FILE REGISTRY
=======================

Introduce:

LocalModelArtifact

Fields:

id
source
repo
revision
filename
format
size_bytes
digest
license
architecture
parameter_count
quantization
created_at
verified_at

============================================================
11. GGUF REGISTRY
=================

GGUF is first-class but not the only future format.

Track actual metadata where available.

Do not infer model capabilities solely from GGUF filename.

============================================================
12. MODEL ACQUISITION PROVIDER
==============================

Create:

ModelSource

Potential adapters:

LocalFileSource
HuggingFaceSource
OllamaSource

Do not hardcode Hugging Face into model domain.

============================================================
13. HUGGING FACE DOWNLOAD
=========================

Use current official Hugging Face Hub APIs/tooling if implemented.

Support revision-pinned acquisition.

Prefer downloading only required files.

Do not download an entire repository when one GGUF is sufficient.

============================================================
14. MODEL REVISION PINNING
==========================

Record:

repo
revision/commit
filename
digest

A model benchmark must remain attributable to exact artifact.

============================================================
15. GATED MODELS
================

Detect gated/authenticated model requirements.

Do not claim:

NO-COST LOCAL

means:

NO ACCOUNT EVER REQUIRED.

If model is gated:

report:

AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED

and do not bypass gating.

============================================================
16. MODEL LICENSE SAFETY
========================

Read model metadata/license.

Classify:

KNOWN
CUSTOM
UNKNOWN

Do not automatically classify every downloadable model as:

open source
commercially usable

Display limitations.

============================================================
17. NO AUTO-DOWNLOAD BY DEFAULT
===============================

Discovery may recommend models.

It must NOT automatically download large files.

Require explicit:

zcoder models pull ...

or equivalent.

============================================================
18. DOWNLOAD PLAN
=================

Before download show:

model
source
revision
file
size
free disk
license
gated status
estimated fit

============================================================
19. DRY RUN
===========

Support:

zcoder models pull MODEL --dry-run

No network/file mutation.

============================================================
20. RESUMABLE DOWNLOAD
======================

Use upstream cache/resume behavior where supported.

Do not re-download identical model unnecessarily.

============================================================
21. DOWNLOAD INTEGRITY
======================

Validate digest where authoritative digest exists.

Record actual file hash otherwise.

A corrupted/incomplete artifact must not become VERIFIED.

============================================================
22. STORAGE QUOTA
=================

Configure local model storage limit.

Before downloading:

available disk
current cache
requested model

Warn/fail according to policy.

============================================================
23. MODEL CACHE
===============

Centralize model artifact cache.

Do not duplicate 10 GB model for every project.

Project profile references immutable model artifact.

============================================================
24. CACHE CLEANUP
=================

Provide:

zcoder models cache
zcoder models prune

Never delete model currently in use.

Dry-run supported.

============================================================
25. HARDWARE PROFILE V2
=======================

Expand HardwareProfile.

CPU:

architecture
physical/logical cores
instruction capabilities where safely detectable

Memory:

total
available

GPU:

vendor
device
VRAM
runtime availability

Storage:

free disk
model cache disk

============================================================
26. HOST BENCHMARK
==================

Measure basic local host capacity without an LLM:

CPU throughput proxy
memory bandwidth proxy where practical
disk throughput only if safe

Avoid intrusive benchmarks.

============================================================
27. MODEL FIT ESTIMATOR V2
==========================

Estimate:

weights memory
KV cache
context memory
runtime overhead

Inputs:

quantization
context length
batch
parallel slots
offload configuration

Output:

FITS_COMFORTABLY
FITS
MARGINAL
DOES_NOT_FIT
UNKNOWN

============================================================
28. SAFETY MARGIN
=================

Never consume 100% RAM/VRAM intentionally.

Configurable margins:

min_free_ram
max_ram_percent
max_vram_percent

============================================================
29. CPU-FIRST PROFILE
=====================

For CPU-only machines:

prefer appropriately quantized smaller models.

Do not recommend 70B model solely because catalog labels it high quality.

============================================================
30. QUANTIZATION PROFILE
========================

Normalize quantization metadata.

Do not rank quantization purely by bit count.

Benchmark actual behavior where possible.

============================================================
31. QUANTIZATION RECOMMENDER
============================

Inputs:

RAM/VRAM
quality preference
speed preference
task
runtime

Output:

candidate quantizations

with reasons.

============================================================
32. LLAMA.CPP AUTO-TUNING
=========================

Audit CURRENT llama.cpp runtime flags first.

Build controlled tuning abstraction for parameters such as:

context
threads
batch
parallel slots
GPU offload
KV behavior
memory mapping
flash-attention-like features where documented
speculative decoding where supported

Never generate flags unsupported by current runtime.

============================================================
33. TUNING PROFILE
==================

Persist:

RuntimeTuningProfile:
model_artifact
hardware_fingerprint
runtime_version
parameters
benchmark_version
score

============================================================
34. HARDWARE FINGERPRINT
========================

Profile key should include enough host characteristics that a tuning
result from one machine is not silently used on incompatible hardware.

============================================================
35. RUNTIME VERSION FINGERPRINT
===============================

Record:

llama.cpp version/build
Ollama version
vLLM version

Tuning result may become stale after runtime change.

============================================================
36. OLLAMA LIFECYCLE
====================

Audit current Ollama API/runtime.

Support:

daemon health
model list
model metadata
pull planning
load/inference
unload where documented

Do not shell out if API provides safer functionality unless needed.

============================================================
37. OLLAMA MODEL IDENTITY
=========================

Use provider-reported digest when available.

Do not benchmark only by mutable model tag.

============================================================
38. VLLM LIFECYCLE
==================

Treat vLLM primarily as configurable serving backend.

Do not auto-install CUDA/ROCm drivers.

Inspect hardware compatibility before recommending it.

============================================================
39. VLLM HARDWARE ELIGIBILITY
=============================

Use current official vLLM hardware/quantization matrix.

A runtime/model combination that current vLLM does not support:

INELIGIBLE

not:

maybe.

============================================================
40. GENERIC SERVER PROFILE
==========================

For generic OpenAI-compatible server:

declare capabilities explicitly or probe.

Do not assume:

# OpenAI-compatible

complete OpenAI feature parity.

============================================================
41. PROVIDER CAPABILITY PROBE
=============================

Create optional probes:

CHAT
STREAMING
TOOLS
STRUCTURED_OUTPUT
EMBEDDINGS

Use bounded tiny requests.

No probe may accidentally call commercial fallback.

============================================================
42. CAPABILITY DATABASE
=======================

Persist capability result by:

model artifact
runtime
runtime version
probe version

============================================================
43. BENCHMARK TOURNAMENT
========================

Create:

ModelTournament

Input:

candidate local models
task profile
hardware
cost policy

Run bounded benchmark suite.

Rank by measured result.

============================================================
44. TOURNAMENT TASK PROFILES
============================

Initial:

CODING_SMALL
CODING_REPAIR
TOOLS
STRUCTURED_OUTPUT
RAG_QUERY

No enormous benchmark suite.

============================================================
45. SCORING
===========

Use objective measures.

Coding:

tests fixed
validation
unwanted diff
attempt count

Tools:

schema correctness
tool selection
arguments

Performance:

TTFT
tokens/sec
wall time
peak memory

============================================================
46. QUALITY VS SPEED
====================

Keep separate scores:

correctness
latency
memory
tool reliability

Then derive task-specific ranking.

Do not hide tradeoffs behind one opaque number.

============================================================
47. BENCHMARK REPEATS
=====================

Support multiple runs to reduce noise.

Report:

median
variation
sample count

Do not claim statistically strong results from one run.

============================================================
48. MODEL WARMUP
================

Separate:

cold start
warm inference

in measurements.

============================================================
49. PEAK MEMORY
===============

Measure approximate peak host memory where feasible.

Do not present estimate as exact VRAM telemetry.

============================================================
50. BENCHMARK FAILURE
=====================

Model failure remains data.

Do not exclude failed model from report.

Record:

timeout
OOM
invalid tool call
test failure

============================================================
51. AUTOTUNING SEARCH
=====================

Search only bounded safe parameter combinations.

Do not brute-force hundreds of expensive configurations.

============================================================
52. EARLY STOPPING
==================

Stop tuning candidate when:

OOM
severe slowdown
quality regression
timeout

============================================================
53. BEST PROFILE
================

Persist best profile per:

model
hardware
task

Do not create one universal tuning profile.

============================================================
54. PER-PROJECT MODEL PROFILE
=============================

Create:

.zcoder/models.yaml

or appropriate equivalent.

Example concept:

coding:
policy: zero
runtime: auto
model: auto

review:
runtime: auto
model: auto

embedding:
model: ...

Do not force exact filename if existing project config architecture is
better.

============================================================
55. AUTO MODEL
==============

Support:

model=auto

Resolution:

project requirements
→ policy
→ hardware
→ installed models
→ capability evidence
→ benchmark history
→ selected model

============================================================
56. MODEL EXPLAIN
=================

Provide:

zcoder models explain --task coding

Output:

selected model
runtime
fit
benchmark
capabilities
cost
rejected candidates

============================================================
57. NEVER AUTO-SPEND
====================

Under zero-cost profile:

if no suitable local/free model exists:

NO_ELIGIBLE_ZERO_COST_MODEL

Do not invoke paid provider.

============================================================
58. OPTIONAL FREE REMOTE
========================

FREE_REMOTE may be supported only when pricing/access has explicit
current evidence.

Unknown is not free.

============================================================
59. MODEL DOWNLOADER UX
=======================

Commands may include:

zcoder models search
zcoder models info
zcoder models pull
zcoder models remove
zcoder models list
zcoder models cache

Follow current CLI architecture.

============================================================
60. MODEL SEARCH
================

Do not scrape random model websites.

Use supported model source APIs.

Allow filters:

format
size
task
license metadata
gated status

============================================================
61. RECOMMENDED DOWNLOAD
========================

Provide:

zcoder models recommend-download

based on host profile.

Return several candidates, not one absolute answer.

============================================================
62. NO SILENT DOWNLOAD
======================

Recommendation is not execution.

User/operator explicitly triggers acquisition.

============================================================
63. GGUF MODEL FACTORY
======================

Where tooling allows, support registration of user-provided GGUF.

Do NOT implement quantization conversion from arbitrary models unless
the existing stack genuinely supports it safely.

============================================================
64. QUANTIZATION CONVERSION BOUNDARY
====================================

If conversion/quantization support is implemented:

make it optional.

Record:

source artifact
tool version
quantization
output digest

Never overwrite original weights.

============================================================
65. MODEL BUILD REPRODUCIBILITY
===============================

For locally produced artifacts record:

input digest
command/config
tool version
output digest

Do not claim bit reproducibility unless tested.

============================================================
66. SPECULATIVE DECODING
========================

If current runtime supports it:

treat as optional optimization.

Benchmark:

target only
vs
target + draft

Only enable when measured improvement exists.

============================================================
67. DRAFT MODEL FIT
===================

Account for draft model RAM/VRAM too.

Do not recommend speculative decoding if combined memory becomes unsafe.

============================================================
68. CONTEXT AUTO-TUNING
=======================

Do not automatically use model maximum context.

Select context based on:

task
RAG
hardware
memory

Larger context can reduce performance/memory headroom.

============================================================
69. RAG-AWARE CONTEXT
=====================

Use local repository retrieval to avoid oversized context.

Benchmark:

larger raw context
vs
smaller context + RAG

where useful.

============================================================
70. LOCAL EMBEDDING FACTORY
===========================

Upgrade TF-IDF architecture without making neural embeddings mandatory.

Support:

TFIDFEmbedding
LocalModelEmbedding

Choose based on:

availability
quality
cost
hardware

============================================================
71. EMBEDDING BENCHMARK
=======================

Benchmark repository retrieval quality with deterministic fixtures.

Measure:

recall@k
MRR or another justified ranking metric

Do not benchmark only latency.

============================================================
72. LOCAL RERANKING
===================

Optional local reranker adapter.

No hosted reranker required.

If absent:

RAG still works.

============================================================
73. INDEX PROFILE
=================

Persist:

embedding provider
model digest
dimension
chunk strategy
index version

============================================================
74. INDEX INVALIDATION
======================

Invalidate/rebuild when:

embedding model changes
chunking changes
branch/base changes materially

============================================================
75. LOCAL MODEL DAEMON MANAGER
==============================

Introduce service manager boundary.

It may manage ZCoder-owned runtime processes.

Do not terminate user-owned Ollama/vLLM process.

============================================================
76. OWNERSHIP
=============

Every managed runtime process records:

owner=ZCODER
pid
process fingerprint

External process:

owner=EXTERNAL

Lifecycle semantics differ.

============================================================
77. LOAD / UNLOAD POLICY
========================

Keep models loaded based on:

RAM pressure
recent use
configured idle timeout

Do not keep every model resident.

============================================================
78. MEMORY PRESSURE REACTION
============================

On low memory:

do not start another large local model.

Queue/pause/fail gracefully.

============================================================
79. CONCURRENT INFERENCE
========================

Benchmark concurrency safely.

Determine per-profile:

max parallel requests

Do not assume CPU-only host handles many parallel generations well.

============================================================
80. JOB SCHEDULING + MODEL CAPACITY
===================================

Scheduler should understand local model slots.

Prevent 10 jobs from launching 10 copies of same 7B model.

============================================================
81. SHARED MODEL SERVER
=======================

Multiple jobs may safely share server where runtime supports it.

Respect:

parallel capacity
tenant/workspace isolation
context separation

============================================================
82. TENANT SECURITY
===================

Shared local model server must not leak prompt/history between jobs or
tenants.

Add isolation tests.

============================================================
83. LOCAL MODEL LOGGING
=======================

Do not log full source/prompt by default.

Diagnostics should be privacy-conscious.

============================================================
84. OFFLINE GUARANTEE V2
========================

Strict offline profile permits:

loopback
local filesystem
local subprocess

No internet.

Model acquisition obviously requires network unless model already
exists.

Separate:

OFFLINE_EXECUTION
from
ONLINE_MODEL_ACQUISITION

============================================================
85. AIR-GAPPED MODEL IMPORT
===========================

Support registering model from local file.

Verify:

digest
format
metadata

No internet required.

============================================================
86. AIR-GAPPED RUNTIME
======================

Run:

local file
→ llama.cpp/local runtime
→ coding job

with network interception proving no outbound traffic.

============================================================
87. REAL LOCAL INFERENCE EVIDENCE
=================================

Highest priority.

If llama.cpp or Ollama can be installed/available in environment:

run actual local inference.

Do not substitute FakeRuntime.

Record:

runtime
runtime version
model
model digest
hardware
latency
result

============================================================
88. REAL CPU MODEL TEST
=======================

Prefer a small model that realistically fits host.

Do not download a huge model just to obtain E4.

Test:

chat
stream
structured response
coding mini benchmark

where model supports each capability.

============================================================
89. REAL TOOL-CALL TEST
=======================

Only mark TOOL_CALL_REAL PASS if actual model produced valid tool call.

Otherwise:

NOT_SUPPORTED
or
FAILED_QUALITY

============================================================
90. REAL AUTONOMOUS REPAIR
==========================

Create deterministic temporary repo.

Introduce controlled bug.

Actual local model:

inspect
plan
edit
test
repair if needed
validate

Record exact result.

No FakeRuntime.

============================================================
91. QUALITY FAILURE IS ACCEPTABLE
=================================

If small CPU model cannot solve repair task:

report failure honestly.

Do not weaken benchmark to force PASS.

The platform may still pass runtime integration.

============================================================
92. MODEL SUCCESS THRESHOLD
===========================

Separate:

RUNTIME_VERIFIED

from:

CODING_QUALITY_VERIFIED

A model can produce valid inference but fail coding benchmark.

============================================================
93. MODEL FACTORY TEST MODE
===========================

No automatic large download in PR CI.

Use:

unit/contract tests

plus optionally scheduled:

REAL_LOCAL_MODEL

test.

============================================================
94. REAL LOCAL RELEASE PROFILE
==============================

Define:

LOCAL_RUNTIME_VERIFIED

Requirements:

actual local server
actual model
actual generation
zero paid calls

Define stronger:

LOCAL_CODING_VERIFIED

Requirements additionally:

real autonomous coding repair succeeds.

============================================================
95. CPU-ONLY PROFILE
====================

Create explicit:

CPU_LOCAL

release evidence.

Do not make GPU necessary.

============================================================
96. GPU PROFILE
===============

GPU remains:

NOT_TESTED

until real GPU runner exists.

============================================================
97. AMD / NVIDIA / APPLE
========================

Architecture supports them through HardwareProfile/runtime capabilities.

Do not claim verified acceleration without hardware evidence.

============================================================
98. WINDOWS
===========

Model runtime paths/process handling must be portable.

Test mocked/platform-specific code.

Actual real-model Windows test optional unless runner exists.

============================================================
99. MODEL LICENSE REPORT
========================

`zcoder models info` should show:

source
license identifier/status
gated
digest
size
runtime compatibility

Do not provide legal conclusions.

============================================================
100. SUPPLY CHAIN
=================

Treat model artifact like executable dependency.

Record provenance metadata.

Warn on digest change for same mutable tag.

============================================================
101. MUTABLE TAG DETECTION
==========================

If:

same provider tag
different digest

mark benchmark/tuning results stale.

============================================================
102. TUNING INVALIDATION
========================

Invalidate auto-tuning profile when:

model digest changes
runtime version changes
material hardware fingerprint changes
benchmark definition changes

============================================================
103. MODEL PROFILE EXPORT
=========================

Support portable JSON/YAML profile containing no secrets.

Useful for reproducing setup on another similar host.

============================================================
104. PROFILE IMPORT
===================

Imported profile must be revalidated against actual hardware.

Do not blindly trust imported tuning.

============================================================
105. BENCHMARK EXPORT
=====================

JSON/CSV.

Include:

model identity
runtime
hardware
settings
results
benchmark version

